# checks/ holds the reader scripts AND the data they are run against - pasted
# Pine Logs, CSV dumps, whatever a session happened to produce. The code is the
# project; the data is a snapshot of one morning and does not belong in it.
#
# A WHITELIST rather than a list of data extensions, so a dump saved tomorrow
# under an extension nobody thought of is ignored by default instead of being
# committed by accident.
checks/*
!checks/*.js
!checks/*.mjs
!checks/*.cjs
!checks/*.mts
!checks/*.ts

# Hand-made backups of the Pine files - mid-session snapshots kept for
# recovery, never part of the project. Same reasoning as the data above: they
# stay on disk, git simply stops asking about them.
*.bak*
